{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Deriv"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.a4_magnitude_one_scalar_gate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.a4_magnitude_one_scalar_gate","kind":"theorem","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L324-L352","doc":"**(CAPSTONE) The A=4 ≥4-body magnitude is a ONE-SCALAR gate — WALL(scope-(a)) — and\nthe naive uniform per-pair magnitude is scope-(b) EXCLUDED.**\n\nWith the derived exchange spectrum `{±√5, ±1}` fixed (`detG_eq_spectral_product`), the\nmagnitude functional `b₄ = −ln det(I + G)`:\n\n1. **surjects onto `(0, ∞)`** (`magnitude_form_surjective`): every positive AME target is\n   reachable ⇒ the magnitude is **NOT scope-(b) excluded**; but the reaching `m` is a\n   function of the target (an anchor-inversion = FIT) ⇒ **NOT closed** — no identified\n   categorical driver fixes `m`.  This SHARPENS the #4526 reweight bracket: the obstruction\n   is not the bracket width but that the single scalar `m` is free.\n2. **is strictly monotone** on `(0, 1/√5)` (`b4_strictMono_on`) ⇒ the gate is *exactly one*\n   scalar and the required `m` is unique.\n3. **excludes the naive uniform `z ≈ 0.499`** (`naive_z_unphysical`): `5z² > 1` ⇒\n   `det < 0`, unphysical — a scope-(b) exclusion citing the proved spectrum.  Direct analog\n   of the #4526 geometric OVERSHOOT ⇒ the surviving mechanism is a categorical principle\n   fixing `m` strictly BELOW the naive `z` (equiv. a normalized `W` strictly below\n   `d_q²/D²`).\n\nNothing is wired; `μ₄`/`B(⁴He)`/`b₄` are never inverted into production; `free_parameters\n= 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.documented_targets_all_reachable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.documented_targets_all_reachable","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L310-L320","doc":"Documented A=4 magnitude targets (probe constants; TARGETS, never inverted into\nproduction): the `[1⁴]` connected cumulant `b₄ ≈ 9.243 MeV`, the 4-body simplex residual\n`|μ₄| ≈ 4.591 MeV`, and the full binding `B(⁴He) ≈ 28.296 MeV`.  Each is positive, hence\neach is reachable by `magnitude_form_surjective` via a target-dependent `m` (a fit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.magnitude_form_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.magnitude_form_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L280-L306","doc":"**(MAIN) The derived magnitude form is SURJECTIVE onto `(0, ∞)` in its one free\nscalar.**  For every positive target `t`, there exists a per-pair bond magnitude\n`m ∈ (0, 1/√5)` (equivalently `5m² < 1`) with `b₄(m) = t`, given by the closed form\n`m = √((6 − √(16 + 20·e^{−t}))/10)`.\n\nConsequence for the A=4 program: because `b₄(m)` attains EVERY positive value, matching an\nAME target (`b₄ ≈ 9.243 MeV`, or `|μ₄| ≈ 4.591`, or `B(⁴He) ≈ 28.30`) does not constrain\nthe framework at all UNLESS an independent categorical driver fixes `m`.  The witness `m`\nhere is a function of the target `t` — an anchor-inversion = **FIT** — so this is a\nreachability (NOT scope-(b) excluded) statement, never a derivation and never wired. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG_mStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG_mStar","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L266-L278","doc":"**`det(I + G)(√(u*(D))) = D`** for `D ∈ (0,1)`: the closed-form `m = √u*` hits any\nprescribed determinant value `D`.  Uses `(√u)² = u` and the root identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.uStar_mem_Ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.uStar_mem_Ioo","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L246-L264","doc":"For `D ∈ (0,1)`, the root `u*(D)` lies strictly in `(0, 1/5)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.uStar_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.uStar_root","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L236-L244","doc":"`u*(D)` is a root: `5·u*² − 6·u* = D − 1`.  Algebraic, using `√(16+20D)² = 16+20D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.uStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.uStar","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L232-L234","doc":"The closed-form inverse `u*(D) = (6 − √(16 + 20D))/10` — the smaller root of the\nquadratic `5u² − 6u + (1 − D) = 0` in `u = m²`.  For `D ∈ (0,1)` it lies in `(0, 1/5)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.b4_strictMono_on","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.b4_strictMono_on","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L221-L228","doc":"**`b₄` is strictly INCREASING on the physical region** (the gate is exactly one\nscalar; the required `m` is unique). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG_strictAnti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG_strictAnti","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L207-L219","doc":"**`det(I + G)` is strictly DECREASING on the physical region.**  For\n`0 < m₁ < m₂` with `5m₂² < 1`, `det(m₁) > det(m₂) > 0`.  Purely algebraic:\n`det(m₁) − det(m₂) = (m₂² − m₁²)·(6 − 5(m₁² + m₂²))`, and both factors are positive since\n`m₁² + m₂² < 2/5 < 6/5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.b4_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.b4_pos","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L200-L205","doc":"**`b₄` is strictly positive on the physical region** `(0, 1/√5)`: `det ∈ (0,1)` there,\nso `log det < 0`, hence `b₄ = −log det > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.b4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.b4","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L196-L198","doc":"The connected 4-body cumulant magnitude in the derived form: `b₄(m) = −ln det(I + G)`,\nthe attractive branch (positive on the physical region). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.zD_unphysical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.zD_unphysical","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L179-L192","doc":"**(SCOPE-(b), convention-D, whole q-window) The canonical convention-D naive\nper-pair magnitude `z_D = q³/(q²+1)` is unphysical for EVERY `q ∈ [1, 7/5]`.**\n`det(I + G)(z_D) < 0`, because `5·z_D² > 1` (above the writhe ceiling `1/√5`)\nwhile `z_D² < 1`.  This is the convention-D analog of `naive_z_unphysical` (which\ncited the *excised* convention-C value `0.499`): under the CANONICAL Markov\nconvention the overshoot is *larger* — `z_D(q₀) ≈ 0.613 > z_C(q₀) ≈ 0.499` — so\nthe exclusion is strengthened, and it now holds across the entire `|q| > 1`\nphysical window, not just at the substrate point.  Cited invariant: the exchange\nspectrum `{±√5, ±1}` fixing `det = (1 − 5m²)(1 − m²)` (`detG_eq_spectral_product`).\nThe surviving mechanism must therefore fix `m` strictly BELOW the naive braiding\noverlap under **either** Markov convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.zD_sq_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.zD_sq_mem","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L154-L177","doc":"On the physical window `1 ≤ q ≤ 7/5` the convention-D naive magnitude sits\nstrictly **above** the writhe ceiling and **below** `1`: `1/5 < z_D² < 1`.  Both\nbounds are polynomial (`q⁴ + 2q² + 1 ≤ 4q⁶ < 5q⁶` for the lower; `q⁶ < q⁴+2q²+1`\non the window for the upper).  The window comfortably contains the substrate\n`q₀ ≈ 1.110`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.zD_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.zD_sq","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L150-L152","doc":"`z_D(q)² = q⁶/(q²+1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.zD","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L142-L148","doc":"The **canonical convention-D** naive per-pair (Markov) bond magnitude\n`z_D(q) = q³/(q²+1)` (owner ruling 2026-08-15 R1: convention D is canonical, C\nexcised).  The `naive_z_unphysical` theorem above used the *excised* convention-C\nvalue `z_C(q₀) ≈ 0.499` as a bare rational; this is its canonical-convention\nreplacement, stated symbolically in `q` and proved on the whole window rather\nthan at a point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.naive_z_unphysical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.naive_z_unphysical","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L131-L138","doc":"**The naive uniform per-pair magnitude `z ≈ 0.499` is UNPHYSICAL (scope-(b)).**  The\nframework's naive bond factor `z = 0.499320334` (probe\n`b4-1four-complete-graph-writhe-signs`, constant `z_bond_factor`) satisfies `5z² > 1`\n(`z` exceeds the writhe cap `1/√5 ≈ 0.447` by ~12%), so `det(I + G)(z) < 0` and the\nattractive `−ln det` branch does not exist there.  Direct analog of the #4526 geometric\nOVERSHOOT: the naive categorical value runs PAST the physical window. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG_neg_of_above_ceiling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG_neg_of_above_ceiling","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L119-L129","doc":"**The derived ceiling structurally excludes `m ≥ 1/√5` (within the framing `m < 1`).**\nIf `1/5 < m²` and `m² < 1`, then `det(I + G) < 0`: the first factor `1 − 5m²` is negative\nwhile `1 − m²` is positive.  Cited invariant: the exchange spectrum `{±√5, ±1}` fixes the\nmost-negative scaled eigenvalue at `−m√5`, giving `det = (1 − 5m²)(1 − m²)`.  This is a\n**scope-(b)** exclusion of any per-pair magnitude at or above the writhe cap `1/√5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG_mem_Ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG_mem_Ioo","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L106-L117","doc":"**Physical region.**  For `0 < m` with `5m² < 1` (i.e. `m < 1/√5`), the determinant is\nstrictly between `0` and `1`.  `0 < det` is physicality; `det < 1` makes `b₄ = −ln det`\nstrictly positive (an attractive/binding contribution). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG_expand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG_expand","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L100-L102","doc":"Polynomial normal form `det(I + G) = 1 − 6m² + 5m⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG_eq_spectral_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG_eq_spectral_product","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L91-L98","doc":"`det(I + G)` is exactly the product over the four spectral eigenvalues `{±m√5, ±m}`.\nThis is the derivation of `detG` from the exchange spectrum (not an assertion of a value):\n`∏ (1 + λᵢ)` with `λ ∈ {m√5, −m√5, m, −m}` telescopes to `(1 − 5m²)(1 − m²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4InterfaceMagnitude.detG","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4InterfaceMagnitude.lean#L83-L89","doc":"The determinant `det(I + G)` for the ⁴He `[1⁴]` complete-graph exchange matrix `G`\nwhose EXACT spectrum is `{±√5, ±1}` (derived in #3924, probe\n`b4-slater-antisymmetrizer-exchange-sign`): with per-pair bond magnitude `m`, the\neigenvalues of `G` are `{±m√5, ±m}` and\n\n  `det(I + G) = (1 + m√5)(1 − m√5)(1 + m)(1 − m) = (1 − 5m²)(1 − m²)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}